#
#
#-- Menu top fill (square corners) --#
# CC: The list's top strip. This used to draw the rounded-corner glyphs (S/U/V/T
# CC: in font 6); now it fills the strip flat, so the menu top corners are square.
# CC: %Vf(031835) forces the theme BACKGROUND colour (the dynamic engine swaps it
# CC: to the album dominant just like the list body) -- a bare %dr would paint the
# CC: foreground colour and leave a light block above a dark menu. On the backdrop
# CC: (%VB), which clear_viewport memcpys from for the first row; leaving it
# CC: unpainted is what clipped the top row. Foreground line stays empty.
%Vl(Home_Corners,0,25,-,12,6)%VB%Vf(031835)%dr(0,0,-,-)
%Vl(Home_Corners,0,25,-,12,6)
#
# CC: Panel-narrow twin (starts at x=120 when the now-playing panel is on screen).
%Vl(Home_Corners_Panel,120,25,200,12,6)%VB%Vf(031835)%dr(0,0,-,-)
%Vl(Home_Corners_Panel,120,25,200,12,6)
#
%Vl(Sub_Menu_Corners,0,52,-,12,6)%VB%Vf(031835)%dr(0,0,-,-)
%Vl(Sub_Menu_Corners,0,52,-,12,6)
#
#--- END ---#
#
#
#--- Scrollbar Engine ---# $SE
# Logic controlling the scrollbars.
#- Image Preloads -#
# CC: Scrollbar image: Thumb = the draggable bar.
# CC: (the flush wipe image is gone -- the viewport is gated in $VD).
%xl(Thumb,Scrollbar_Thumb.bmp)
#
# Use the %?LB in these viewports. If you do it while calling the viewport instead, it bugs drawing out for some reason.
#
#- Right side Tall Scrollbar -#
# CC: Tall (home-menu) right scrollbar track, built from stacked glyphs
# CC: (C top cap, D middle repeated, E bottom cap). The track is enabled in $VD
# CC: unconditionally: the gutter is reserved by the scrollbar SETTING, not by
# CC: whether the list overflows, so when it doesn't overflow the reserved strip
# CC: shows an empty rail instead of nothing at all.
%Vl(Scrollbar_Tall_Right,310,30,5,205,9)%VB
C
D
D
D
D
D
D
D
E
# CC: Foreground twin of the track. The %VB line above paints the backdrop; this
# CC: clears the same rect on the foreground, which is what lets the backdrop
# CC: show through. The thumb's line used to do this job as a side effect, so
# CC: splitting the thumb off took the track's foreground pass with it and the
# CC: rail drew into the backdrop and stayed invisible.
%Vl(Scrollbar_Tall_Right,310,30,5,205,-)
# CC: The thumb lives in its own viewport, gated on %LB in $VD, because it must
# CC: NOT share the track's label. %LB written with bar params parses to
# CC: SKIN_TOKEN_LIST_SCROLLBAR, which sizes itself from selected_item against
# CC: nb_items and never consults needs_scrollbar -- so on a list that fits it
# CC: would draw a slider that moves, which is exactly what the empty track is
# CC: meant to replace.
%Vl(Scrollbar_Tall_Right_Thumb,310,30,5,205,-)%LB(0,0,5,205,invert,noborder,nobar,slider,Thumb)
#
#- Left side Tall Scrollbar, shifted right of the panel -#
# CC: Same track and thumb as above, moved from x=5 to x=125 so it sits beside
# CC: the narrow menu instead of underneath the panel. This is the "scrollbar
# CC: on the left" case: with the panel occupying the left of the screen, the
# CC: left edge of the LIST is x=125, not the left edge of the screen.
%Vl(Scrollbar_Tall_Left_Panel,125,30,5,205,9)%VB
C
D
D
D
D
D
D
D
E
%Vl(Scrollbar_Tall_Left_Panel,125,30,5,205,-)
%Vl(Scrollbar_Tall_Left_Panel_Thumb,125,30,5,205,-)%LB(0,0,5,205,invert,noborder,nobar,slider,Thumb)
#
#- Left side Tall Scrollbar -#
%Vl(Scrollbar_Tall_Left,5,30,5,205,9)%VB
C
D
D
D
D
D
D
D
E
#
%Vl(Scrollbar_Tall_Left,5,30,5,205,-)
%Vl(Scrollbar_Tall_Left_Thumb,5,30,5,205,-)%LB(0,0,5,205,invert,noborder,nobar,slider,Thumb)
#
#- Right side Short Scrollbar -#
%Vl(Scrollbar_Short_Right,310,57,5,173,9)%VB
C
D
D
D
D
D
D
%Vl(Scrollbar_Short_Right,310,230,5,5,9)%VBE
#
%Vl(Scrollbar_Short_Right,310,57,5,178,-)
%Vl(Scrollbar_Short_Right_Thumb,310,57,5,178,-)%LB(0,0,5,178,invert,noborder,nobar,slider,Thumb)
#
#- Left side Short Scrollbar -#
%Vl(Scrollbar_Short_Left,5,57,5,173,9)%VB
C
D
