#--- END ---#
#
#
#--- Now Playing Panel ---# $NP
# CC: Enabled from $VD only while a track is loaded and a cover was found.
# CC: The panel owns x=0..119, left of the menu, matching the WPS so the two
# CC: screens read as the same design. Widgets_Backdrop fills that strip;
# CC: Miniplayer_Widget is a 4px rail in the FOREGROUND colour along the art's
# CC: top, right and bottom edges, rounded at the two RIGHT corners. The art is
# CC: square (111x111) so covers are scaled whole rather than centre-cropped,
# CC: and runs flush off the left edge of the screen -- there is no left rail,
# CC: so that side is square and the block reads as a tab off the screen edge.
# CC: 111 is the largest that keeps the menu its full width: the list starts at
# CC: x=123 and the rail stops at x=114, the same 8px clearance the panel had
# CC: on its other side before it moved.
# CC: Art + title + artist are centred as one block in the area below the
# CC: status bar (y=25..239): 119 + 4 + 40 + 2 + 18 = 183 tall, leaving a 16px
# CC: margin top and bottom, so the block starts at y=41.
#
%Vl(Widgets_Backdrop,0,25,120,-,-)%VB%Vf(031835)%dr(0,0,-,-)
%Vl(Widgets_Backdrop,0,25,120,-,-)
#
# CC: The frame is a solid foreground-coloured box drawn before the art, which
# CC: then covers all but the three rails. It goes on the backdrop like the art
# CC: does, because the corner viewports below clear back to the backdrop -- a
# CC: foreground-only frame would be erased the moment they are declared.
%Vl(Miniplayer_Widget,0,41,115,119,6)%VB%Vf(fff2f9)%dr(0,0,-,-)
%Vl(Miniplayer_Widget,0,41,115,119,6)
#
%Vl(Miniplayer_Album_Art,0,45,111,111,9)%VB%Cl(0,0,111,111,c,c)%Cd
vvvvv
vvvvv
vvvvv
vvvvv
%Vl(Miniplayer_Album_Art,0,45,111,111,-)
#
# CC: The rounded right corners are subtracted in two passes. s and v are the
# CC: outer wedges, painted in the BACKGROUND colour at the frame's own corners
# CC: to round the frame; t and u are the smaller inner wedges, painted in the
# CC: FOREGROUND colour at the art's corners so the art's square corner is
# CC: replaced by rail colour. The two radii differ by roughly the rail width,
# CC: which is what keeps the curves an even 4px apart all the way round.
# CC: Outer first -- the inner viewports overlap them, and declaring a viewport
# CC: clears it. These wedges sit at the RIGHT of the 14px cell, so a viewport
# CC: starts 13 columns left of the edge it rounds (114-13, 110-13); the bottom
# CC: pair also sit at the bottom of the 30px cell, so those start 29 rows above
# CC: it (159-29, 155-29).
%Vl(Miniplayer_Widget,101,41,14,30,6)%Vf(031835)
s
%Vl(Miniplayer_Widget,101,130,14,30,6)%Vf(031835)
v
%Vl(Miniplayer_Widget,97,45,14,30,6)%Vf(fff2f9)
t
%Vl(Miniplayer_Widget,97,126,14,30,6)%Vf(fff2f9)
u
#
# CC: Now-playing panel: %wt title box (bottom-aligned) with the artist in the
# CC: smaller font 4 below, matching the WPS. A 1-line title sits at the box
# CC: bottom right above the artist; a 2-line title grows up. No single/dual
# CC: decision, nothing desyncs. Box sits below the framed art (which ends y=160).
# CC: The panel is filled with the theme BACKGROUND (031835) and the text drawn
# CC: in the theme FOREGROUND (fff2f9). Both are written as the theme's own
# CC: configured colours so the dynamic engine maps them -- it matches on exact
# CC: colour, sending fg to the accent and bg to the dominant album-art colour.
# CC: x=4 keeps the text off the screen edge the art runs flush to, and lines it
# CC: up with the inner face of the bottom rail.
%Vl(Panel_Title,4,164,110,40,3)%Vf(fff2f9)
%wt(%it,bl,%fn)
%Vl(Panel_Artist,4,206,110,18,4)%Vf(fff2f9)
%?if(%St(scroll speed),=,1)<|%s>%aL%?ia<%ia|%d(1)>
